+# slice markov_w2[d S : (d + 1) S] (S = the lm_head's
+# vocab-parallel shard, 20480 at TP8: 21 MB instead of 168 MB), each step runs the
+# step kernel on the rank's own lm_head logits shard (no pre-step logits gather),
+# publishes (max key, token) per row through the drafter's Lamport mailbox
+# (``comm.DrafterComm.exchange_rows``, per-step slots) and every rank selects the
+# same token (``_exchange_select``). The biased logits shards of the k steps are
+# gathered once after the last step (``comm.gather_logits``, the bytes the pre-step
+# gather moved) and scattered into the draft logits cache rows for the rejection
+# sampler, which reads the full vocabulary. VLLM_MOET_MARKOV_SHARD=0 keeps the
